cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the ReCoSoC 2019 paper below, which
  introduces the metric it is built on. The MOCAST 2020 paper, which introduces
  the online control, is listed under references.
title: >-
  omp-energy-rl: online reinforcement-learning control of OpenMP energy
  efficiency
abstract: >-
  Measures a parallel application's own progress from inside the OpenMP runtime
  (chunks per second and chunks per Joule), detects its execution phases with
  an autoencoder, and uses reinforcement learning to choose core count and clock
  frequency while the application runs, with no prior profiling and no source
  annotation.
type: software
